From c6b80493467f015eae634298ec6dcbe4a720f1d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:11:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): hand Update to hermes-sync on hosts it manages
 instead of an idle-only update [daveey]

Desktop's Update / Try again ran its own detached `hermes update`, which only pauses idle gateways, so it
failed every time a chat was busy ("Hermes couldn't finish updating ... busy or cannot acknowledge an idle
pause", laptop-1 2026-11-20). On a host whose core updates hermes-sync applies (fresh window record), the
client and backend Update now post hermes-sync's existing Force-update request, which pauses busy chats and
continues them after the update, and the dialog says so ('synced' stage). Hosts hermes-sync does not manage,
or backends too old to answer, keep the old path. POST /api/hermes/update refuses on a managed host as a
backstop for older clients; GET /api/hermes/update/force reports `managed`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
